 "caption": "Nobody was ever supposed to see this.\n\nIn 1819, Goya, 72 and completely deaf, bought a country house outside Madrid. It was already called the House of the Deaf Man, after a previous owner. Over the next few years he covered its walls with 14 nightmares, now called the Black Paintings. He never titled them and never showed them in public.\n\nThis one, Saturn Devouring His Son, was painted downstairs, in the room historians think was his dining room.\n\nHalf a century later a banker had the murals peeled off the walls, tried to sell them in Paris, and ended up donating them to the Prado.\n\n🖤 Would you eat dinner next to it?",
